pvs_cad_num: THEORY
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% pvs_cad with NASALib's interval arithmetic: in a theory
% that imports this one, (cad) and (cad *) also enclose the constant real
% terms that interval arithmetic evaluates (pi, e, sin(1), ln(2), atan(1),
% ...) between two rationals, proved by NASALib's (numerical), when the
% decision with them as unknowns does not prove the goal.  With trans_bounds,
% sin, cos, exp, ln and atan of terms with constants of
% the sequent (sin(x) for a skolem constant x) get polynomial bounds, and
% enclosures over the ranges the hypotheses give the constants.  pvs_cad
% itself leaves interval_arith@strategies out, so that numerical's
% expression language (the constructors X, ADD, SUB, MULT, POW, DIV, ...,
% and its lemmas) and its conversions (r2E, I2E, b2B, interval2str, and
% structures' val2some) are not added to every theory that imports pvs_cad;
% the interval type itself (Interval, lb, ub, ##, with the conversion
% Member?) comes in through alg_isign either way.  Without this import,
% (cad) says when such a term could be enclosed.
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
BEGIN
  IMPORTING pvs_cad, interval_arith@strategies, trans_bounds
END pvs_cad_num
